# NeuroScope-Web — frontend environment
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Only VITE_-prefixed variables reach the browser bundle, and everything in
# this file IS bundled into client-side JavaScript. Never put a secret here.
#
# This file previously documented ~22 feature flags (VITE_ENABLE_ATTENTION_VIZ,
# VITE_USE_QUANTIZED, VITE_NUM_WORKERS, a VITE_HF_TOKEN, …). None of them were
# ever read by any code in src/. They have been removed rather than left as
# aspirational config — the single variable below is the complete, verified
# surface, matching `grep -r "import.meta.env" src/`.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend API base URL
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read in src/lib/api.ts. Falls back to http://localhost:8000 when unset, which
# is what `uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000` serves locally.
#
# For the deployed frontend, point this at the HuggingFace Space, e.g.
#   VITE_API_BASE=https://ethan-sam-neuroscope-api.hf.space
#
# Whatever value you set here must also appear in the backend's ALLOWED_ORIGINS
# (Space → Settings → Variables and secrets), or every request fails CORS.
# VITE_API_BASE=http://localhost:8000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not configured here
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HF_TOKEN — required for the gated Llama-3.2 models, but it is a BACKEND
# secret. Export it in the shell running uvicorn, or set it as a Space secret.
# It must never be given a VITE_ prefix; that would ship your token to every
# visitor's browser.
#
# Dev-server port (3001), COOP/COEP headers, and worker/build settings are not
# env-driven — they are literals in vite.config.ts.
